                      (    forth6809.asm):01629         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):01630         ; RTSCHECKLO - called from mainline code (KEY), NOT from the
                      (    forth6809.asm):01631         ; ISR, so it must mask IRQ around its critical section: IRQH's
                      (    forth6809.asm):01632         ; own TXOFF path also writes ACIACR, and an interrupt landing
                      (    forth6809.asm):01633         ; mid-decision here could otherwise race it. If the ring has
                      (    forth6809.asm):01634         ; drained to INLOWATER or below and RTS is currently high,
                      (    forth6809.asm):01635         ; reassert RTS low - restoring TX-interrupt-enable too if
                      (    forth6809.asm):01636         ; output happens to be queued, since the ACIA has no control
                      (    forth6809.asm):01637         ; byte combination offering RTS-high with TX-interrupt-enabled
                      (    forth6809.asm):01638         ; simultaneously (see CR_RTSHI's comment).
